BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Visit Davis": "https://visitdavis.org/event/art-in-action-lovely-landscapes/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:visitdavis
X-SOURCE:Visit Davis
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261025T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261025T150000
DTSTAMP:20261016T173023Z
CREATED:20260916T183030Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20261016T173023Z
UID:10003062-1792933200-1792940400@visitdavis.org
SUMMARY:Art in Action: Lovely Landscapes
DESCRIPTION:Art in Action: Lovely Landscapes in Davis \nSunday\, October 25\, 1-3 PM \n$5 Members\, $10 Non-Members (per person\, all materials included) \nCreate the landscape of your dreams! Inspired by Danilo Campos’ exhibit\, draw and paint your very own landscape on canvas and craft a decorative frame for your painting with cardstock\, gold paint\, and ribbon. \n  \nHow it works: \nArt in Action engages kids in art projects that are fun\, creative\, and collaborative with their family members. This is a drop-in program for ages 5-12. No registration in advance is required\, but space and supplies are limited to the first 25 participants and are available on a first come\, first served basis. When you arrive\, pay with cash or card at the front desk. A parent or adult caregiver is required to stay\, but only has to pay for the project for themselves if they are also doing art. Stay as long or as short as you like over the two hour period.  \n  \nWe have a different Art in Action family workshop every month. Learn more at https://pencegallery.org/art-in-action/. \n  \nThis monthly program is generously sponsored by Mary Stephens DeWall & Les DeWall.
URL:https://visitdavis.org/event/art-in-action-lovely-landscapes/
LOCATION:Pence Gallery\, 212 D Street\, Davis\, CA 95616
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://visitdavis.org/wp-content/uploads/Art-in-Action-logo-18-j1ixtp.jpg
ORGANIZER;CN="Pence Gallery":MAILTO:pencesocialmedia@gmail.com
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Visit Davis": "https://visitdavis.org/event/open-mic-and-music-trivia-halloween-themed/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:visitdavis
X-SOURCE:Visit Davis
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261025T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261025T200000
DTSTAMP:20261016T173033Z
CREATED:20261015T173025Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20261016T173033Z
UID:10003094-1792951200-1792958400@visitdavis.org
SUMMARY:Open Mic and Music Trivia Halloween Themed
DESCRIPTION:This month’s theme for Open Mic & Music Trivia in Davis is Halloween.  Come in costume\, sing songs about Halloween or anything else ghoulish spooky\, or witchy.  Of course\, if you don’t want to play-a-long and just do your own thing\, you are still welcome! \nWhether you’re looking for a venue to share your own talents or just looking to enjoy hearing (and seeing) some local performers\, we invite you to this free monthly event. We provide the sound\, stage and lights – the rest is up to you. Play us your favorite song\, tell us some jokes\, act out a scene from your favorite play with friends. \nWe will continue to feature our Music Trivia contest throughout the evening in between acts. The winner will receive a $20 Watermelon Music gift card! \nWe ask that each performance be suitable for an all-ages venue\, and that you arrive on time and stay until the end to support your fellow performers. \nFREE!!!\nDoors open/sign-ups @ 5:30.\nFirst act @ 6:00. \nPlease help support the Watermelon Music with your purchase of a drink or a snack at Open Mic!  Non-alcoholic drinks and pre-packaged snacks are available for sale at The Melon Ball.  (Cash or Venmo only) \nWe hope to see you there!
URL:https://visitdavis.org/event/open-mic-and-music-trivia-halloween-themed/
LOCATION:The Melon Ball – Watermelon Music\, 1970 Lake Blvd.\, Davis\, CA\, 95616\, United States
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://visitdavis.org/wp-content/uploads/OctOpenMic-U1GzhZ.jpg
ORGANIZER;CN="Watermelon Music":MAILTO:info@watermelonmusic.com
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Visit Davis": "https://visitdavis.org/event/healing-arts-one-time-workshop-8/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:visitdavis
X-SOURCE:Visit Davis
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261026T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261026T114500
DTSTAMP:20261016T173024Z
CREATED:20260909T180022Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20261016T173024Z
UID:10003049-1793008800-1793015100@visitdavis.org
SUMMARY:Healing Arts One-Time Workshop
DESCRIPTION:Healing Arts One-Time Workshop in Davis \nMonday\, October 26\, 10-11:45 AM \n$5 Members\, $10 Non-Members (all materials included) \n  \nPart of the Pence’s Healing Arts Program and run by facilitator Amy Vidra\, this one-time workshop focuses more broadly on themes related to depression\, anxiety\, or major life changes. Through the process of art making\, participants will have opportunities for discussion\, education\, and connecting with peers in a safe and supportive space. \n  \nRegistration is required in advance through our website\, and space is limited to the first 8 participants who register. Participants must be 18 or older\, and no art experience is necessary. This program is generously sponsored by Bob & Joanne Andresen. \n  \nRegister here (REQUIRED): https://pencegallery.org/education/programs/workshops-and-classes/ \n  \nIf you register for this session and are unable to attend\, please let us know in advance. \n  \nAny questions? Email pencegallery@gmail.com.
URL:https://visitdavis.org/event/healing-arts-one-time-workshop-8/
LOCATION:Pence Gallery\, 212 D Street\, Davis\, CA 95616
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://visitdavis.org/wp-content/uploads/Healing_Arts-copy-22-OAr19D.jpg
ORGANIZER;CN="Pence Gallery":MAILTO:pencesocialmedia@gmail.com
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Meetup Mindful Embodied Spirituality": "https://www.meetup.com/mindful-embodied-spirituality/events/316877051/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:meetup_mindful_embodied_spirituality
X-SOURCE:Meetup Mindful Embodied Spirituality
UID:event_316877051@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20261017T014132Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261026T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261026T200000
SUMMARY:Conscious Conversations & Somatic Practices  
DESCRIPTION:Iama Embodied Community\nThis is a spiritual community that ho
 nors the body’s wisdom and lived experience. Whether you’re healing fr
 om religious trauma\, deconstructing beliefs\, exploring spirituality\, or
  just want to be with other conscious persons\, this space is for you.\n\n
 Expect conscious conversations\, meditation\, breathwork\, sound healing\,
  and other somatic practices to help reconnect with ourselves and each oth
 er.\n\nwe share a potluck dinner every last Monday of the month.\n\n📅 *
 *Date & Time**: Mondays 6-8 PM\n📍 **Location**: 727 T St. Sacramento\, 
 Ca\, 95811\n💜 **All our events are free\, donations supported.**\n✨ *
 *No prior experience or spiritual beliefs necessary.**\n📩 **RSVP/ Quest
 ions? Reach out at** embody.iama@gmail.com\n🔗 **Follow us on Instagram:
 ** [@embody.iama](https://www.instagram.com/embody.iama)\n\nPS: we meet in
  the social hall of Parkview Presbyterian Church. Please find us through t
 he back entrance\, the brown gate on Solons alley. You may park in the bac
 k\, move the orange post to park and please return it when you leave.
